1785545078770522	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy9gQ		item.comment	bn-2s6q	{"body":"RFC 0037 expanded from 193 to 408 lines as a normative specification (commit df8be49 in .maw/workspaces/bn-2s6q). New sections: Versioning and revision (closed vocabularies, schema_epoch/SD-08, CPNF versioning as an epoch advance, intent epoch vs schema epoch); Registry record and status machine (proposed/accepted/superseded, transitions + authority); Intent bundles (contents/identity, import I1-I6, acceptance chain A1-A5 incl. acceptance-replay binding, three-way merge M1-M7 with a precise independence definition); Fields (full type/required/policy-key table, per-group enum table, absence/null/default rules, well-formedness W1-W10); Canonical identity ID1-ID8 with a closed exclusion list; Change policy (verb semantics as (denied relations, acceptance authority), verb applicability matrix, enforcement P1-P7 incl. accept-time recomputation, verb restrictiveness lattice and policy joins); Revision procedure R1-R9 with compare-and-set concurrency; Corrections (11) and Flags (11); expanded Acceptance vectors. CPNF-1 N1-N9 and S1-S3 preserved verbatim, plus additive reconciliation (fairness condition is a bare state formula, identifier/binder/literal types). KNOWN FIX applied: capitalized Unknown at old lines 152/164 corrected to lowercase, plus Proposed->proposed and Conflict->conflict, each recorded with direction. Validator: uv run --with jsonschema python3 tools/validate_dossier.py => status pass, SD-05 still derived paid. No plan.md, schema, RFC 0026/0031, or ledger edits; validation-results.json/VALIDATION_REPORT.md untouched."}	blake3:_5Bu7YpEF49pexJQBBno5oMk4YEbHrkqe1WB6tLnWbA
1785545089573546	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy9wQ		item.comment	bn-23m	{"body":"Implemented PR-2 bullets 1-2 in crates/continuum-value/src/value.rs (new module alongside epoch.rs/assurance.rs; lib.rs updated). Committed d9cca79 in .maw/workspaces/bn-23m, synced onto epoch e44daf7.\n\nDOMAIN: the 16 kinds of notes/plan/schemas/cir.schema.json $defs.value (INV-003 — the schema decides), which is Revision 2 §5.3's value system narrowed to the exact and finite: null, boolean, nat, int, bitvec, bytes, string, symbol, tuple, seq, set, multiset, record, variant, map, opaque. Options are variants; relations/graphs are sets of tuples; comprehensions and symbolic predicates are expressions, not values. No floating point (RFC 0037 'Floating-point literals are excluded from v1 so the canonical encoding stays byte-deterministic').\n\nENCODING (CVNF-1, named parallel to RFC 0037's CPNF-1): one-byte kind tag (0x01..0x10; 0x00 reserved) plus a self-delimiting, prefix-free payload built from two order-preserving primitives — nat(n) = [len][minimal BE magnitude], int(n) = 0x01++nat(n) or 0x00++complement(nat(-n)). Sorted sets/maps/records and normalized integers per RFC 0001 'Serialization'. BTreeMap/BTreeSet only; no HashMap anywhere; no floats; stdlib only; no new dependency edges.\n\nPRIMARY: the encoding. ADR-0013 makes canonical structural encoding the identity, and RFC 0037 N4 orders by 'the byte ordering of their own N8 encodings' — so Ord is DEFINED as lexicographic order on CVNF-1 bytes and computed structurally without allocating. Consequence documented: sequences/strings/bytes compare shortlex (length first), so \"z\" < \"aa\"; a test pins Ord against encode() on every pair so the two cannot drift. Value deliberately has no Hash impl (ADR-0013: identity must not depend on collision improbability; also makes HashMap iteration over values unrepresentable).\n\nREJECTION: constructors reject duplicate record fields, duplicate map keys, duplicate/zero multiset multiplicities, bad bitvec widths/out-of-range bits, non-ASCII or empty names, and over-deep nesting; set construction dedupes because {1,1}={1} is set theory, not canonicalization. Value::decode is written as the docs/33 trust-base component: rejects non-minimal integers, negative zero, unsorted or repeated set elements/map keys/record fields, zero multiplicity, out-of-range bitvec, invalid UTF-8, unknown tags, trailing bytes, over-deep nesting; never allocates on an attacker-declared length; reports an over-wide integer as typed-unsupported (IntegerTooWide), not malformed, so a later wider carrier reads today's bytes unchanged. MAX_DEPTH=64, set a measured 4x below the observed dev-profile stack floor.\n\nTESTS: 92 in the crate. Round-trips for every kind + integer boundaries (i128::MIN/MAX, u128::MAX); order laws exhaustive over a ~65-value sample domain (reflexive, antisymmetric, total, transitive); order/encoding agreement on every pair; encoder injectivity (docs/10 obligation); prefix-freeness; determinism across construction orders for set/record/map/multiset; constructor + decoder rejection cases; 29 golden byte vectors pinned with the epoch note that changing one is a §4.6 event, not a fix.\n\nSCOPE FENCE HELD: no content-address computation, no CAS publication, no collision-injection tests — those stay with bn-277 and bn-210. Value::encode() is the byte string bn-277 will digest.\n\nGATE: fmt-check, lint (clippy -D warnings), test (92 pass), boundaries, dossier all EXIT=0. 'just lean' (added to just check by bn-1ee03 after this bone started) fails identically on trunk — elan/Lean toolchain is not installed on this machine; environment bootstrap, not this change."}	blake3:0hwsWraQUQc0e07qq74m4uq16Xfx46QYJNfxsrC6LE4
