1785547343205008	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyrAU		item.comment	bn-2wu5j	{"body":"Applied RFC 0026's flagged minimal IDL fixes in ws bn-2wu5j (commit b307df2). F5: StaleSnapshot added to task.resume and repair.resume errors clauses. F6: evidence.verify response gains 'redacted: Redacted optional' (same shape as evidence.get). F7: new 'rule errors.defect_emission' (next to errors.common/unsupported_surface) requiring a defect_* on ReplayDiverged / parity mismatch / engine crash / explanation-validation failure and its handle in artifacts; program.replay response gains 'defect: DefectHandle optional'. F4: open items 1 and 2 rewritten as resolved by RFC 0026 'Capability administration' / 'Delegation and expiry defaults' (corrections 20/21), entries kept so history stays visible; item 3 untouched. F12: section-5 preamble now attributes ExplanationLevel to RFC 0039 alone and Portfolio to docs/55. idl_version 1.0 -> 1.1 with a new 'Revisions:' note in its doc comment. RFC 0030 F6 line now records the obligation as declared by RFC 0026 as of 2026-07-31 (correction 18), flag history kept. Validator: status pass. CONCERNS: (1) the two new optional fields are compatible changes under rule versioning.compatible_change, which requires raising the protocol minor - version left at 3.0 (RFC 0026 pins 3.0 throughout and is out of fence); the 1.1 revision note flags this for the protocol sweep rather than taking it silently. (2) RFC 0026's F4/F5/F6/F7/F12 flag text and its line 43 'idl_version (1.0)' are now stale and need a follow-up revision of RFC 0026."}	blake3:TlUh7cTfqCbgnKcLH4d80d30O0Eu-ikax2HY1uhmjEI
