1785547655732367	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyrwU		item.comment	bn-7kj	{"body":"SD-10 paid. docs/41 regenerated (133 -> 541 lines) in ws bn-7kj as the non-normative guide around RFC 0032 + repair-transaction/promotion-receipt schemas: twelve gates by name with per-gate reading notes, five gate statuses (no not_applicable, budget exhaustion leaves pending), phase-b/c/d/default profiles with not_yet_enforced, derived-never-asserted status derivation (failure dominates inconclusiveness; gate 12 is the promotion step), change kinds + reclassification, eight neighborhood strategies with disclosure rules and the FR-05 counting rule by reference only (ratified marked quote left unique to research/33 and plan 24.5), evidence floor/swarm append rules, cost ceilings (BudgetExhausted vs QuotaExhausted, Conservative vs Validated reuse), promotion + receipt + rollback, two worked examples keyed to schemas/examples/repair-transaction.example.json (rt_demo1 phase-b ready -> promoted receipt_demo1) and a blocked exact-overfit case, seven failure modes -> gates, RFC 0032 flags F4/F6/F8/F9, a historical nine-step -> gate map so 'docs/41 step n' citations still resolve. Removed the RepairTransaction struct (correction 14), 'block with ReplayDiverged' (correction 6), and 'protected intent is unchanged' (correction 8). plan 25 ledger line flipped to 'SD-10 (paid, PR 0)'; traceability regenerated (spec-debt 14/14 satisfied, 793 active reqs). validate_dossier.py: status pass, spec_debt open [] — pre-freeze open-debt set is now empty. Commit 1a692e7. Not merged/pushed; bone state untouched. Concerns: RFC 0032 line 19 and correction 14 still say SD-10 'remains open' (RFC fenced, needs a follow-up sweep); promotion-receipt.example.json still names two diff identities against correction 10."}	blake3:FJFkTLEqTl6HiS9Rke0KvmsH5MjpodIyAMru9HVurH0
1785547746353546	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEysAU		item.comment	bn-7kj	{"body":"Landed @ a931513. SD-10 paid — check_spec_debt open set now EMPTY (all 14 paid), PR 0's debt exit condition met. Two follow-ups recorded on close: (1) RFC 0032 has two stale self-references calling SD-10 open (Summary + correction 14 tail) — routed to the RFC sweep; (2) schemas/examples/promotion-receipt.example.json violates RFC 0032 correction 10 (semantic_diff/intent_diff name different diff_* identities) — schema+example must be swept together; routed to bn-1lfek's lane or a follow-up."}	blake3:mRchDwXqnLk-erv2L-OBRlCQkQtaxnXyOkokKB6r8SI
