1785548110641625	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyswU		item.comment	bn-21dd	{"body":"G0-DX-13 falsification campaign complete (workspace bn-21dd, commit 6284f91). VIOLATION FOUND — the pass condition does not hold under concurrent garbage collection.\n\nAttacks (crates/continuum-workspace/tests/dx13_falsification.rs, 14 tests, up to 48 threads, outcomes-only assertions): doubled contention (32 publishers x 12 rounds); mixed identical+distinct payloads in one store; identical bytes across three artifact classes; abandoned stagings and crashes-between-the-commits interleaved with successes; refusals injected at every publication phase (Staging/CommittingContent/CommittingIndex) under contention; four-family and total identity collisions under contention; readers + fsck racing publication; idempotent replay (128 receipts); capability mint/revoke racing publication. All twelve held; stable over 10 repeats and under 1- and 2-core pinning.\n\nVIOLATION: ReferenceStore::collect_garbage derives its root set from the index alone, so a publication between commit_content and commit_index is not a root. GC reclaims content the publisher has already been told is durable; the publisher then commits its index entry and gets a receipt for an artifact that read() refuses and fsck reports as MissingReferent — the defect class publication.rs documents as 'never produced by this store's own ordering'. With a colliding identifier it is worse: deleting the in-flight content also deletes the value ADR-0013 exact comparison was about to compare against, so publisher A's receipt ends up naming publisher B's bytes. Three reproductions retained, #[ignore]d so just check stays green (two deterministic via the StorageFaults rendezvous, one unassisted): cargo test -p continuum-workspace --test dx13_falsification -- --ignored. src/ NOT patched — the fix needs a follow-up bone. Falsifies three documented claims: INV-017 visibility ordering (visible with no content), collect_garbage's 'cannot make a published artifact unavailable', and docs/35's root set ('named roots, live tasks, receipts, retention policy' implemented as index entries only).\n\nMutation matrix (dx13_mutation_campaign.rs, 6 tests): index-before-content caught by the atomic-abort check; last-writer-wins receipts caught by the no-lost-receipts check (and by the collision check's receipt count); overwrite-on-collision caught by the exact-comparison check; faithful re-implementation control passes all three, as does the real store. Each catch asserts which complaint fired.\n\nRecords: notes/plan/spikes/R3_SPIKE_REPORT.md §9 (mirrored into docs/53_SPIKE_FINDINGS_REV3.md); G0 matrix row 21 Evidence cell now cites the campaign and the failure. Status/Decision cells left unchanged — reclassifying the row cross-checks against plan.md §0.3 and is the lead's call. just check: PASS end to end. plan.md untouched, so no traceability regen."}	blake3:nWLPMBdL9OWgZtGrmX_ZIRbeVaK3DWYAB8vQaQlOo-E
1785548161948815	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEytAU		item.comment	bn-1lfek	{"body":"Schema sweep landed in ws bn-1lfek (2 commits: bbfff8d schemas+examples, 6e60d5b docs/41 known-gaps). No schema_epoch advances anywhere — every document stays at epoch 1 with its $id unchanged, under schemas/README.md's rule that epoch 1 is a draft edited in place until PR 5 freezes the interface. Each item classified by what it WOULD have cost after the freeze.\n\nDONE — context-pack.schema.json (RFC 0028): F1 PRIORITY additive — optional nullable 'parent' (^ctx_), so a pack family is reconstructible from artifacts and the ratified FR-01 'counting every expansion' byte sum is computable; left optional (requiring it is breaking, and F1 asks for a lineage field not a required one), with a $comment recording that RFC 0028's interim evidence-graph obligation stands until the field is REQUIRED, since an absent parent is still indistinguishable from an unrecorded one. F3 additive — optional 'compiler' block (compiler_version required within, nullable ranker_id for the stage-9-disabled fallback, ranker_config). F4 would-be-breaking — content_budget now required, bytes required within it, tokens now requires tokenizer_id. F5 would-be-breaking — both relation fields now carry the closed 11-member ExpansionRelation enum. F12 would-be-breaking — omissions[].expandable required, and expandable:false must carry redaction/unsupported.\n\nDONE — promotion-receipt.schema.json (RFC 0032): F8 would-be-breaking — coverage was additionalProperties:true, now a closed six-group object (replay/neighborhood/property_mutation/defect_mutants/refinement_coverage/certificate_rebuild/incremental_parity) matching the RFC's composition row and gate table; the neighborhood group carries per-strategy explored/failing/truncated over the closed 8-member §8.3 strategy set, a frontier required whenever truncated, and the failing_neighbors array the ratified FR-05 counting rule is stated over — each entry naming neighbor + strategy class + run handle, so adequacy is gradeable mechanically. F9 would-be-breaking — reuse_provenance $def (reuse-edge class + function_id/function_version, RFC 0030's quarantine triple), attachable per strategy and per mutation campaign and REQUIRED whenever a strategy reports reused>=1; Experimental is omitted from the class enum for the same reason gates[].status lists two of five statuses — it cannot support promotion, so it is unrepresentable here. New root conditional derived from the receipt's own gate list: neighborhood 'passed' forbids a truncated strategy. Correction 10 (coordinator addition): the example now names one diff identity in both semantic_diff and intent_diff; the agreement rule itself is a sibling-value comparison draft 2020-12 cannot express, so it lives in both descriptions and is the surviving half of F7.\n\nDONE — semantic-diff.schema.json (RFC 0031): F1 would-be-breaking — intent_changes[].unit locator, required for the 11 field members whose unit-of-classification table declares a per-unit key; the 4 whole-field members (bounds, trust_boundaries, completion_policy, assurance) have no sub-unit. F2 would-be-breaking — requested_assurance is now the 5-member AssuranceLevel enum. F3 additive — optional 'classifier' block (classifier_version + cpnf_version).\n\nDONE — intent-contract.schema.json (RFC 0037): F4 would-be-breaking — the 15 policy keys now carry per-field verb restrictions encoding the closed W6 matrix, so no-decrease on properties or no-downgrade outside assurance is unrepresentable. F5 would-be-breaking — scope.fragments minItems:1 (W3). F11 additive text — description no longer writes the wire literal in prose case. F3 half paid — policy_reviewers keys restricted to the 15 policy keys and empty principal lists rejected. F10 (intent-registry-record) additive + one conditional — optional nullable supersedes/superseded_by (^in_) so M1's common ancestor is recoverable, and a 'superseded' record must name a non-null successor.\n\nDEFERRED with reasons — RFC 0031 F4 (typed policy.reasons): needs a closed per-field reason vocabulary RFC 0031 does not mint; minting one in the schema would make the schema the source of a vocabulary the RFC does not define. The schema-side half is paid instead by 'unit'. Recorded in a $comment on policy.reasons. RFC 0037 F1 (unit-key uniqueness) and F2 (referential integrity): not expressible — uniqueItems compares whole items and there is no cross-document reference keyword; both stay checker rules. RFC 0037 F3 second half (review verb => non-empty reviewers): a relation between one object's keys and another's values, needing 15 hand-written conditionals. RFC 0037 F6/F7/F8/F9: RFC-level, new artifact class, or IDL. RFC 0032 F6/correction 11 (policy_decision/coverage/unknowns required): breaking, and it pairs with the transaction-side policy_verdict requiredness — both sides should land together. RFC 0032 F1-F5: IDL or repair-transaction surfaces. RFC 0028 F2 (per-item guarantee attribution — C4 is the interim rule and a per-item label changes what a selected item means), F6/F10 (IDL), F7/F11 (wire outcome/verdict vocabulary), F8 (crashpack), F9 (checker attribution — needs a vocabulary RFC 0028 does not mint).\n\nExamples regenerated: context-pack (correction 2's omitted_noise_events relation and correction 3's tokens-only budget, plus parent/compiler/tokenizer_id; the omission and its expansion query now agree at 196 items), promotion-receipt (typed coverage incl. a Conservative reuse record; correction-10 diff identity), semantic-diff (classifier, unit), intent-registry-record (explicit null lineage). docs/41's known-gaps section updated to record F8/F9/correction-10 as paid (coordinator's ask).\n\nValidation: uv run --with jsonschema python3 tools/validate_dossier.py => \"status\": \"pass\", 19 schema pairs, spec-debt open list empty. Plus 32 ad-hoc mutant checks confirming each new constraint rejects what it is meant to reject (free-string relation, missing expandable, budget without bytes, tokens without tokenizer, non-ctx parent, properties record without unit, bogus AssuranceLevel, no-decrease on properties, empty scope.fragments, unknown/empty policy_reviewers, truncated-with-passed-neighborhood, truncated without frontier, reused without provenance, Experimental class, unknown strategy token, failing neighbor without run handle, extra coverage group, superseded without successor).\n\nCONCERNS for follow-up (all fenced out of this bone): (1) RFC 0028 line ~46 says 'The schema's sixteen required properties' and lists content_budget as optional, while its own F4 flags exactly that as the gap and another sentence calls content_budget required — paying F4 makes it seventeen, so that sentence and the optional/required list need an RFC 0028 edit. (2) RFC 0028 F1/F5/F12 and RFC 0031 F1-F3 and RFC 0037 F3-F5/F10 and RFC 0032 F8/F9 are now paid; their Flags entries should be struck or marked paid in the owning RFCs. (3) schemas/examples/semantic-diff.example.json still violates RFC 0031's unchanged-shortcut MUST: before_intent == after_intent == in_ack_v1 with a non-empty intent_changes. Not flagged by RFC 0031 and not fixable without either deleting the dossier's only intent_changes demo or minting a second intent identity (which ripples into the promotion-receipt example's diff/policy story), so left alone deliberately. (4) schemas/README.md untouched — its 'epoch 1 is a draft, edited in place' paragraph already licenses every narrowing above, so no convention note was needed."}	blake3:jSMdVvxWF-uSu82raRKSKA7F9j_JDqre0zhX7BtgEj8
1785548283005927	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEytQU		item.comment	bn-21dd	{"body":"Landed @ a46c21e. Campaign verdict: 12 outcome attacks held; one GENUINE violation — collect_garbage derives its root set from the index alone, so a publication between commit_content and commit_index is invisible to GC and its content is reclaimed (receipt for unreadable artifact; sharper witness: receipt naming another publisher's bytes via collision + GC). All three retained repros verified failing by the lead before merge. Lead decisions: DX-13 flips back to Open — freeze-blocking (pass condition 'no lost receipts' has a verified failing repro; flip is free since DX-10/DX-14 already block freeze, reverses when the fix lands); fix bone created for the GC root set (pin in-flight publications at commit_content + receipts per docs/35); PR-2 exit evidence (bn-1sh6) additionally blocked on that fix."}	blake3:7ZXKuN0eKYG1f3T03wwIdfvl6EXIYBYjbBGANzuLMzA
1785548283038257	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEytgU		item.move	bn-21dd	{"state":"done"}	blake3:8W7GI0WHXoMk-vOrrEqR5fHu8To7_NLrySUNn6WR-m0
1785548299845025	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEytwU		item.create	bn-2siid	{"description":"# Context\nbn-21dd's G0-DX-13 falsification campaign found a genuine violation: ReferenceStore::collect_garbage (crates/continuum-workspace/src/publication.rs:~1325) derives its root set from the index alone. A publication that has completed commit_content but not commit_index is invisible to GC, so its content is reclaimed while the publisher holds a durability promise — the publisher then commits its index entry and receives a receipt for an artifact that cannot be read (fsck: MissingReferent). Sharper witness: with a colliding identifier, GC deletes the operand of ADR-0013's exact comparison, and a second publisher's byte-different value lands at the first publisher's identity — publisher A's receipt names publisher B's bytes, fsck clean. docs/35 specifies the root set as named roots, LIVE TASKS, RECEIPTS, and retention policy; the implementation omits in-flight publications and receipts.\n\nThree failing reproductions are retained #[ignore]d in crates/continuum-workspace/tests/dx13_falsification.rs (run: cargo test -p continuum-workspace --test dx13_falsification -- --ignored). Two are deterministic via the StorageFaults rendezvous; one is unassisted multicore.\n\n# Direction (not prescriptive)\nRoot set must include in-flight publications (e.g. a pin registered at commit_content, released at commit_index/drop) and receipts, per docs/35. Keep the no-ambient-nondeterminism discipline — no clocks, no epoch guesses.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The three #[ignore]d reproductions pass and the #[ignore] attributes are removed (they run in the default suite).\n- [ ] StoreDefect::MissingReferent doc claim ('never produced by this store's own ordering') and collect_garbage doc claim ('collecting cannot make a published artifact unavailable') are true again — restore or reword to match the fixed behavior.\n- [ ] The 12 passing DX-13 attack outcomes are unchanged (no regression in dx13_falsification.rs / dx13_mutation_campaign.rs / publication.rs suites).\n- [ ] G0_SPIKE_MATRIX.md DX-13 row: Status returns to Evidence (reference implementation), Evidence cell updated to record the falsification-and-fix cycle; plan §0.3 counts updated to match (check_g0_matrix_counts grammar).\n- [ ] spikes/R3_SPIKE_REPORT.md §9 and docs/53 mirror gain a resolution note (keep bodies byte-identical).\n- [ ] just check green.","kind":"bug","title":"Fix ReferenceStore GC root set: pin in-flight publications and receipts"}	blake3:p2watKw3QGxfnqqk2F0J0_7ZRcW8is_2abzUYG_Y_sA
