1785548835169880	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyyQU		item.comment	bn-2siid	{"body":"GC root-set fix landed in the workspace (pin taken at commit_content, released when CommittedContent settles). Reproductions 1 and 3 pass unmodified. Reproduction 2 (concurrent_gc_must_not_let_a_receipt_name_another_publishers_bytes) CANNOT pass unmodified, and I believe the line in question is wrong rather than the fix — flagging per instruction before changing it.\n\nThe line is dx13_falsification.rs:1573-1574:\n    let second = store.publish(CLASS, b\"impostor\".to_vec(), &publisher_token(1))\n        .expect(\"the second publication found nothing to collide with\");\n\nThat expectation IS the defect. In the fixed store publisher A's in-flight content 'original' survives the concurrent GC, so it is still there as the operand of ADR-0013's exact comparison, and B's byte-different 'impostor' is necessarily refused with Aborted(CommittingContent, IdentityCollision). There is no correct store in which B still succeeds: B succeeding at A's identity with different bytes either conflates two artifacts (forbidden by ADR-0013 and caught by the mutation campaign's OverwriteOnCollision) or leaves B holding a receipt for A's bytes, which is the same class of lie the test is named after.\n\nChange made (strengthening, not weakening): the .expect on B is replaced by a match that REQUIRES B to be refused with IdentityCollision at CommittingContent and panics if B succeeded; the 'the identifier collides' claim is kept by asserting A's handle is the collider's identity; and the final assertion (A reads back 'original') is unchanged verbatim. Verified against unfixed src/: the modified test still FAILS there (B succeeds -> panic arm fires), so it remains a valid reproduction and now also catches the identity theft the original tolerated.\n\nLead: this is the one place I edited a retained reproduction's body. Revert/redirect if you disagree."}	blake3:ajEYFXlWeDvPtNb45TI8JFLGvnXvAlL5EEQC4ahCTXY
1785549010207081	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyygU		item.comment	bn-26fh	{"body":"RFC 0027 expanded to full normative form in ws bn-26fh (commit f21c929, 62->617 lines; only rfcs/0027-*.md touched, no plan.md edit — consistent with the six prior expansions). STRUCTURE: Status (normative wire artifact + companion sources + landed vocabulary crates/continuum-workspace/src/publication.rs + both ratified frontier rows) / Summary / Precedence (4 ranks + explicit RFC 0026 boundary) / Versioning / The authority ladder (A1-A9) / The admission predicate (T1 level, T2 scope, T3 privilege, T4 validity — conjunction, deny-only) / Capabilities: 8-field descriptor, expiry E1-E3, delegation D1-D9, revocation R1-R3 / The operation authority registry (72 per-operation rows + distribution + R-1..R-5 + per-namespace rationale) / Reconciliation with plan (one-to-one tables for §10.1's 12 principles, §18.2's 6 capabilities + 4 denials, §10.4's 7 adapter obligations, docs/49's 5 roles) / Tool schemas TS-1..TS-7 / Ordering and bounds B1-B8 + capability-relative next_operations N1-N3 / Context policy + closed 11-member ExpansionRelation C1-C4 / Handoff H1-H8 incl. stale-handle table / Privileged boundary P1-P6 / Safety S1-S7 / Denial X1-X5 / Isolation + FR-20 gate mapping / 4 conformance examples (single-agent, handoff, stale-handle, prompt-injection) / Evaluation / Corrections / Rejected / Open questions / Acceptance. REGISTRY-IDL VERIFICATION: machine-checked all 72 rows against the IDL — authority AND annotations token-identical (revise-intent/revise_intent spelling recorded as a mapping, not a change); counts read 18 / propose 8 / execute 40 / revise-intent 4 / promote 2 and readonly 28 / mutation 44 / task_starting 26 / paginated 6 / streaming 2 / privileged 5 / audit_recorded 6, matching RFC 0026 exactly; registry set == plan §10.2 set (symmetric diff empty). No IDL change forced; no IDL edit made. CORRECTIONS (26 + 8 flags, RFC 0031 house pattern with per-item Direction): IDL corrected this RFC 1-7 (per-operation not grouped granularity; revise-intent token mapping; ExpansionRelation is closed not 'initial'; descriptor is 8 fields with numeric delegation_depth; output_policy is optional; authority/@mutation orthogonal BOTH ways — context/evidence.verify/query.clean_compare are @mutation at read, workspace.diff is @readonly at propose; privileged set is 5 and audit_recorded 6 — the old text omitted intent.reject). This RFC decides 8-17 (the four-test admission conjunction; @privileged as a second test not a level — the only way docs/49's 'proposal only' is reachable, since intent.propose_revision is revise-intent and NOT privileged while accept/reject/lock are; request actor MUST equal the presented capability's descriptor actor, mismatch = CapabilityDenied; 'narrower capability' defined as descent + admission-set inclusion; next_operations/recovery are capability-relative; lexicographic tool ordering + filtering is never the auth check; handoff isolation = artifact_classes + creator ownership; expansion never widens scope; the crate's Action::Administer promote floor is not a sixth level; bytes are the graded denominator and the freeze consequence is all three ratified margins). Governs plan/docs 18-26 (ACI lane is research/25 not research/33 — the old 'Baseline ladder (research/33)' was mis-attributed vs plan §24.5; docs/36's nine 'useful relations' vs the closed eleven; docs/36 rule 10's 'Unknown'; docs/36 repair-authority lists; docs/49's matrix has two cells not expressible as levels; docs/49 'proposal only' is a task grant not a default profile; docs/55 carries no authority annotation at all; plan §10.4 evidence-status rule generalized; plan §10.5 sets are ps_/dbg_/forge_). AGREEMENT vs RFC 0026: administration out-of-band at major 3 restated with its obligations; A7 'no operation widens the authority of the connection invoking it'; delegation fail-closed (depth 0 default, D2-D8, child admission set subset of parent); closed four-member actor scheme used and strengthened by the T4 binding; RFC 0026's 'CapabilityDenied decidable from the table' explicitly preserved as a statement about T1 since T2-T4 can only deny. vs FR-20/docs/49: gate-element table maps the three prohibited outcomes, the seven intent-policy blocks, and the eight worker-isolation controls onto ladder rules; refused-AND-recorded is X1∧P5. VALIDATOR: uv run --with jsonschema python3 tools/validate_dossier.py -> 'status': 'pass' (validation outputs untouched; git status clean). NEW FLAGS for bn-2wu5j's IDL fix list (none patched here): F1 CapabilityDescriptor can express only T1+T2 — no field for privileged membership, per-operation deny-list, observe.ingest's production-trace grant, or RFC 0026's capability-scoped sharing policy; F2 instance scope exists only for snapshots/intents so plan §10.5 isolation is class-level only; F3 next_operations/recovery capability-relativity not expressible (composes with RFC 0026 F1); F4 no handshake rejection frame — ServerWelcome is 'on success' only and nothing carries a connection-level ProtocolVersionUnsupported/CapabilityDenied; F5 observe.ingest's second capability undeclared; F6 no adapter mapping manifest so RFC 0026 correction 23 is unenforceable; F7 ResultEnvelope has no audit-correlation identity so a privileged caller cannot cite its own record; F8 store-side vs wire-side administrative floors stated in two places. CONCERNS: (1) F1 is the sharpest — 'default agent capability profile' has no wire representation, so two identical descriptors can differ on whether intent.accept is admitted; T3 is prose until it is paid, and docs/49's Reviewer row stays unenforceable. (2) workspace.diff at propose while @readonly blocks a read-only reviewer from diffing snapshots; left token-identical and raised as an open question (a level move is breaking), with repair.review named as the reviewer path. (3) The T4 actor-binding rule is new normative surface that RFC 0026 does not state; if the protocol leads disagree it should be settled in RFC 0026's connection-lifecycle section rather than here. (4) Workspace was rebased twice mid-task (bn-2wu5j IDL 1.1, then bn-1lfek schema sweep); I re-verified the authority table after each and it was unchanged."}	blake3:nUVuZ7d32OdxFC48siXYpXBgb7uy-eBUJbcxd9cGF20
1785549123045658	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyywU		item.comment	bn-26fh	{"body":"Landed @ f89f65a. Lead independently machine-verified the registry: 72 rows = 72 IDL clauses, sets identical, zero authority/annotation mismatches (revise-intent/revise_intent is the documented hyphen/ident mapping). Distribution read 18 / propose 8 / execute 40 / revise-intent 4 / promote 2 confirmed. Concerns routed: F1–F8 flags + T4 placement question → follow-up bone; F1 (capability profile has no wire representation — T3 unenforceable until paid) and F4/F7 flagged pre-freeze-relevant."}	blake3:hBLHarFvwsYBPp8sBt97MsbC0DB4u5yO4mPFejMJKkk
