1785549163098471	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyzgU		item.create	bn-3ayom	{"description":"# Context\nRFC 0027's expansion (bn-26fh, landed) raised eight new flags against the IDL/protocol, additive to bn-2wu5j's RFC 0026 fix list, plus one placement question. Pattern precedent: bn-2wu5j paid RFC 0026's minimal wire fixes as IDL 1.x.\n\n# Highest-value items (from the expansion's findings)\n- F1 (SHARPEST): 'default agent capability profile' has no wire representation — two identical descriptors can differ on whether they admit intent.accept, so admission test T3 is prose until paid and docs/49's Reviewer row is unenforceable.\n- F4: no handshake rejection frame — likely to matter before PR 5 freeze.\n- F7: no audit-correlation identity on results — likely to matter before PR 5 freeze.\n- T4 actor-binding placement: RFC 0027 states a new normative actor-to-capability binding rule that RFC 0026 (connection lifecycle owner) does not state; decide whether it moves to RFC 0026 or is cross-referenced from it.\n- workspace.diff at propose while @readonly blocks a read-only reviewer (open question in the RFC; a level move is breaking; repair.review named as the reviewer path).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each of F1–F8 dispositioned: paid in the IDL (minor bump per RFC 0026's versioning rules) or explicitly deferred with the deferral recorded in RFC 0027's flag entries.\n- [ ] T4 placement decided and recorded in both RFC 0026 and RFC 0027 (whichever direction).\n- [ ] Registry/IDL token-identity preserved (72 rows; run a mechanical comparison).\n- [ ] Dossier validator green.","kind":"task","title":"IDL/protocol follow-ups from RFC 0027 expansion: F1–F8 triage, T4 placement"}	blake3:n_Lq-kxHUj8inrJwgQ35Iayw2OHwqDeYYqeDpRJsBHc
