1785551193842858	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy9wU		item.create	bn-3ehdm	{"description":"# Context\nFrom bn-1j0i (GOV §1 harness): GOV-1-08 (semantic changes require ADR) and GOV-1-09 (every breaking change increments semantic epoch) are enforced only at their repo-state proxy core today — a single-revision check cannot see that a change happened. Diffing against the merge base makes both genuinely enforceable: a schema whose bytes changed without schema_epoch advancing (past the PR 5 freeze) is a mechanical violation; a semantic-tier src change without a citing ADR/decision-record delta likewise.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A two-revision runner (tools/governance/) that takes a base rev (default: merge base with main) and enforces the delta rules; degrades explicitly (skip + reason) when no base is available, never silently passes.\n- [ ] Violating fixture pairs + self-test per the tools/governance idiom.\n- [ ] gov-1.json evidence entries for GOV-1-08/09 record the strengthened enforcement and drop the proxy-boundary caveat accordingly.\n- [ ] Wired into the governance recipe only when a base rev is resolvable (CI context), documented in README-gov1.md.","kind":"task","title":"Two-revision governance gate: enforce GOV-1-08/09 against the merge base"}	blake3:8oUsrjdA0RvJ7Jebabzf2qtM2lt2DkSlFsZfVRKdji0
