1785552588056011	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyjwY		item.comment	bn-3ayom	{"body":"DECIDED by the user, 2026-07-31: the protocol-minor bump is BUNDLED into this bone's disposition. version stays \"3.0\" with the in-file note until the F1–F8 sweep lands; when this bone pays its wire changes, take the single minor bump (3.0 → 3.1) covering IDL 1.1's compatible fixes AND whatever this sweep adds. Do not bump twice; do not leave the note dangling after the sweep."}	blake3:_3U32rLnf-BpZPNnFb0N2oHO16AsMoPtHEqHW4Gyz8A
1785552670288228	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEykAY		item.comment	bn-2res	{"body":"T02 evidence delivered. New file: crates/continuum-value/tests/t02_reachability_evidence.rs (3 tests, all passing; just check green including Lean/dossier/governance/boundaries).\n\nControl -> evidence map (bone's 4 controls):\n\n1. \"fingerprints are indexes, not identity\" — existing: identity::tests::certified_identity_equality_cannot_consult_a_hash, an_index_under_a_maximally_colliding_hash_still_separates_every_value, a_colliding_lookup_does_not_report_a_false_hit. New: positive_reachable_sets_match_ground_truth_under_every_adversarial_hash (lifts the claim to an actual reachability computation) + negative_a_fingerprint_only_visited_set_loses_reachable_states_under_total_collision (contrapositive: a digest-only visited set demonstrably loses reachable states under the same attack the real mechanism survives).\n\n2. \"exact canonical comparison on collision\" — existing: identity::tests::a_collision_is_counted_rather_than_absorbed, equal_values_get_one_identity_even_when_everything_collides, every_injected_hash_gives_the_same_certified_answers (value layer); publication::tests::an_identity_collision_aborts_rather_than_conflating_two_artifacts, pr2_exit_evidence::negative_artificial_hash_collision_between_distinct_payloads_is_refused_not_conflated, dx13_falsification (concurrency+GC), dx13_mutation_campaign::check_exact_comparison (load-bearing under mutation) (store layer). New: same positive test, plus the bool_pair_diamond fixture, which forces the machinery to tell \"same state via two paths\" (correct merge) apart from \"different state, same digest\" (must not merge) in one run.\n\n3. \"cryptographic digests for artifact identity\" — existing: identity.rs's documented hash seam; Fnv1aPlaceholder is honestly labeled non-cryptographic and tested as such (the_placeholder_declares_itself_non_cryptographic, every_algorithm_token_is_well_formed, a_non_certified_lane_cannot_be_entered_unlabeled). FINDING (not a violation, not patched — src/ out of scope): no cryptographic ContentHasher/ContentIdentifier is vendored anywhere in crates/*/src/ today; only test doubles implement ContentIdentifier repo-wide. This is a pre-existing, already-documented deferral (identity.rs \"Seams left open on purpose\": \"the release hash is not here\"), not a T02 defect — the new positive test proves reachability is identical under a total collider, a partial collider, and the shipped placeholder, so the deferred hash choice can only change performance, never which states are found.\n\n4. \"adversarial collision corpus\" — existing: identity.rs's sample_values/sample_identities against ConstantHash/KindTagHash/LengthHash; dx13_falsification.rs's 12-attack, up-to-48-thread campaign (bn-21dd); dx13_mutation_campaign.rs. New: a second corpus at the reachability layer — 5 state-transition fixtures (no-successor state, self-loop, 5-state cycle, bool-pair diamond DAG, mixed Nat/Record relay) x 2 new local adversarial hashers (TotalCollider, KindByteCollider) + Fnv1aPlaceholder, checked against a hash-free ground truth.\n\nTests (positive/negative/boundary, per delivery checklist):\n- positive_reachable_sets_match_ground_truth_under_every_adversarial_hash\n- negative_a_fingerprint_only_visited_set_loses_reachable_states_under_total_collision\n- boundary_single_state_and_self_loop_graphs_do_not_over_or_under_count_under_collision\n\ndocs/09_THREAT_MODEL.md: checked for a \"delivered:\" annotation convention on threat entries — zero occurrences in that file (the convention exists in notes/START_HERE_IMPLEMENTATION.md for PR items, not in docs/09's threat list). Per scope, left docs/09 untouched rather than inventing a convention. notes/plan otherwise untouched, so no traceability regen was needed.\n\nScope respected: test-only change, one new file under crates/continuum-value/tests/, no src/ edits, no notes/plan edits, no maw ws merge / git push / bn state change. Committed in-workspace: \"test: T02 — hash collision cannot change reachability (bn-2res)\"."}	blake3:tb7NckLxzU-deD511j0aCzFxnIVUgEZzmlN0sK5qkhQ
1785552732732797	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEykQY		item.create	bn-30eym	{"description":"# Context\nT02's control 3 ('cryptographic digests for artifact identity') is a documented deferral, surfaced by bn-2res: no cryptographic ContentHasher/ContentIdentifier exists in any crates/*/src today — only Fnv1aPlaceholder (explicitly labeled a placeholder) and test doubles. identity.rs's 'Seams left open on purpose' section records the seam. Reachability correctness is proven invariant to hash quality (t02_reachability_evidence.rs), so this is about defense-in-depth and PR 6+ daemon-scale identity, not correctness today.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A cryptographic hasher (BLAKE3 or equivalent; dependency-rationale.toml entry with TCB class required) implements the ADR-0013 seam without changing the identity discipline (identity IS canonical bytes; the hash remains an index).\n- [ ] The collision-injection suites still pass unchanged (they must be hash-agnostic).\n- [ ] Fnv1aPlaceholder retained for tests or retired deliberately — decide and record.\n- [ ] T02 control 3 evidence recorded (docs/09 controls satisfied; cite tests + the vendored hasher).\n- [ ] just check green (governance dependency gate included).","kind":"task","title":"Vendor the production content hasher behind the ADR-0013 seam"}	blake3:Jv6rqcFedGGTQ_RJ01eYKl0zpWHPyYtNXku5naAz_1U
