1785554341836077	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyowY		item.comment	bn-2xri	{"body":"Delivered: crates/continuum-workspace/src/components.rs (new module) + crates/continuum-workspace/tests/workspace_descriptor.rs (integration evidence). WorkspaceDescriptor binds ComponentKind::{Source,Dependencies,Toolchain,Configuration} (closed 4-variant enum; Source always present via Snapshot::identity, the other 3 optional). Record grammar: DESCRIPTOR_RECORD_MAGIC|version|count|(tag,handle)* naming components by IDENTITY (Merkle-style, mirrors DirectoryNode); whole-descriptor encode()/decode() carries raw CONTENT per entry (Source's = nested Snapshot::encode() bytes) so decode re-derives every identity, never trusts the wire. Absence is structural: an absent component has no entry at all, not zero bytes — verified by test (empty-but-present vs absent are distinct identities). PartialEq is manual, content-only (source/dependencies/toolchain/configuration fields), identity/record fields excluded — ADR-0013 discipline, same as snapshot.rs's DirectoryNode/FileNode. All identities derived in crate::snapshot::NODE_CLASS (ws_*), reusing the tree's namespace rather than adding a new ArtifactClass. Component records are separately framed (COMPONENT_RECORD_MAGIC|version|kind_tag|len|content) and separately publishable; WorkspaceDescriptor::records() returns source.records() ++ present component records ++ descriptor's own record (children-before-parents), for ReferenceStore composition. 10 inline unit tests (src/components.rs) + 12 integration tests (tests/workspace_descriptor.rs: determinism, component independence, adversarial ConstantIdentity collision, decode rejects truncation/reorder(TagOrder)/unknown-tag/trailing-bytes/missing-source, round-trip across every presence combination, store composition incl. cross-descriptor shared-component convergence). snapshot.rs untouched (read-only consumption of its public API). Gates green: cargo fmt/clippy(-D warnings)/test workspace-wide, check_crate_boundaries, governance (code/ADR/claims), dossier validator, traceability regenerated (PR-3-IMPL-03 flipped active->satisfied), lean build — all pass. START_HERE PR-3 IMPL-03 bullet annotated '(delivered: bn-2xri)'; PHASE-A-DEL-01 left untouched per instructions. just check exit 0. Seams for IMPL-02: WorkspaceDescriptorBuilder::build(source: Snapshot, identifier) takes raw bytes for the 3 optional components — IMPL-02's disk importer decides which on-disk file is 'the' lockfile/toolchain declaration and what constitutes 'configuration' (incl. multi-file concatenation policy), then calls the builder; no ambient file IO happens in this module. Not in scope here (per plan §4.2's other six components): CML modules, Rust semantic extraction, domain-pack manifests, generated correspondence, proof environment, and the governing Intent Contract reference — all left for later PRs/IMPLs, documented explicitly in the module doc so they aren't mistaken for silently-covered ground."}	blake3:gLe4ibkHwQCRfX-6wZ1oOWNjCd6pMWhXqvhUsSAwjnc
1785554409318525	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEypAY		item.comment	bn-1qhe	{"body":"PR-3/IMPL-05 landed in workspace (6932d56). Policy decided in snapshot.rs module doc under one 'byte rule' (a path IS its bytes; the accepted set may not be a function of a Unicode version/locale/platform): Unicode normalization NONE (NFC/NFD are two paths); case EXACT (no folding); non-UTF-8 names REJECTED typed (PathError::SegmentEncoding) rather than escaped, on INV-003 + workspace-snapshot.schema.json typing files[].path as a JSON string; reserved segments = Win32 device stems (CON/PRN/AUX/NUL/COM1-9/LPT1-9, matched on the pre-dot stem under an ASCII-only fold used ONLY for rejection) plus trailing dot/space (PathError::ReservedSegment + ReservedReason); rejected chars extended from {control,backslash,/} to include < > : \" | ? *; new MAX_SEGMENT_BYTES=255 bound (PathError::SegmentTooLong); symlinks OUT of the content model via SymlinkPolicy{Reject, FollowWithCycleDetection} where only Reject is implemented and selecting the other is a typed AdmissionError::UnsupportedSymlinkPolicy; non-regular files refused via Candidate::Special. Deliberate NON-rejection recorded with reasons: case-colliding siblings stay legal (case-sensitive volume is a declared requirement, matching artifact_path.rs), Cf/bidi characters stay legal (rejecting them would key the accepted set to a Unicode general category), hard links need no policy, record grammar + store layout reserve nothing (length-prefixed grammar; store paths derive from handles). ENCODING_VERSION deliberately NOT bumped (grammar unchanged, accepted set only narrowed). Entry point: pub fn admit(candidates: impl IntoIterator<Item=(&[u8], Candidate)>, policy: AdmissionPolicy) -> Result<WorkspaceContent, AdmissionError> — pure and order-independent in BOTH directions (rejection is reported for the least candidate in raw-name order, so two importers of one workspace agree on why it was refused). Plus WorkspacePath::from_bytes as the per-path byte boundary. Tests: 19 new unit tests in snapshot.rs (100 total in the lib) + new tests/deterministic_ordering.rs with 11 acceptance tests; every pre-existing test passes UNCHANGED. just check exit 0 (fmt, clippy -D warnings, tests, boundaries, governance, dossier, lean). START_HERE PR-3 IMPL-05 bullet annotated and traceability regenerated (pr-deliverable 122->121 active). Left to IMPL-02: total rendered-path length (depends on the root prefix), empty directories, and whether the policy in force is recorded beside the snapshot components (IMPL-03)."}	blake3:P3CePEs4cJbAmspvwAni1S0o6bVWECDD8b1ZaOdTang
1785554418521951	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEypQY		item.comment	bn-2xri	{"body":"Landed @ c318e26. Lead verified: 12 integration tests green in-workspace, manual content-only PartialEq confirmed by reading the impl, decode re-derives identities via the caller's identifier, absence-is-no-entry semantics. The explicit out-of-scope list (six remaining §4.2 components incl. the Intent Contract reference) accepted — those ride with PR 4+ bones. Builder seam for IMPL-02 (which on-disk file IS the lockfile, config concatenation policy) recorded."}	blake3:Mg-DHwn3hU0gMuqjTN-EkymA73EB5UzkZI5zDilqI7E
