1785554463429531	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEypwY		item.comment	bn-1qhe	{"body":"Workspace was rebased onto c318e26 (bn-2xri, IMPL-03) mid-run; my commit replayed cleanly on top (no overlap — sibling added src/components.rs + one lib.rs line, I touched only src/snapshot.rs). Re-ran traceability regen on the new base and amended: final commit e9d54d7, PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY now reads pr-deliverable 146/120 satisfied-mapped with 26 delivered, 748 active requirements. just check re-run after the rebase: exit 0."}	blake3:eYfVqr13KXyMUpTzeHbsA16RPPHv5TOTlrM-6eZLS04
1785554648587033	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyqAY		item.comment	bn-1qhe	{"body":"Landed @ 149ea7c. Lead re-ran the FULL workspace suite in-workspace post-rebase (110 lib + all integration suites green — the shared-file replay maw flagged was verified clean). Policy decisions RATIFIED under the byte rule: no normalization, no case folding, non-UTF-8 rejected typed (INV-003: a name with no schema representation cannot be workspace content), Win32 device stems + trailing dot/space rejected on the materialization principle, Cf/bidi accepted (no Unicode-version keying), ENCODING_VERSION correctly NOT bumped (accepted set only narrowed). Known cost accepted and to be documented for users: aux.h/aux.c-style names are refused — correct for a cross-platform content model. Both-direction determinism of admit() (least-rejection in raw-byte order) is the standout. Seam notes for IMPL-02 recorded, incl. policy-in-force beside IMPL-03's components."}	blake3:eCSldDh66d-7H9QWYpxT6BubkkzwCDPukRJo478-g5A
