1785597005194153	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy1wY		item.comment	bn-136f	{"body":"IMPL-02 (assumptions) implemented in crates/continuum-intent/src/assumptions.rs: Assumption{unit,expression,classification?,fidelity_profile?} + AssumptionSet (W1, MAY be empty per RFC 0037), reusing crate::property::PropertyExpression for the same CPNF-1 normal form/identity discipline claims use (RFC 0031 'assumptions': same order as properties, direction inverted). classification/fidelity_profile are undeclared-by-default with no null spelling (RFC 0037: declaredness change != unchanged); encoder omits the key rather than writing null, and this is proven to move the identity in tests. FidelityProfile deliberately carries no Ord (RFC 0002 profiles are unordered). Added AssumptionSet::check_fragments as the W3 analogue of ClaimSet::check_fragments. FLAG for the contract-assembly bone: property.rs's formula/term JSON decoder (decode_formula/decode_term and helpers) is private, so assumptions.rs necessarily carries a second copy of it (built only from property.rs's public surface) rather than editing property.rs, per the workspace fence. Recommend a follow-up bone to extract a shared pub(crate) expression-codec module for property/assumptions/fairness to import. Tests: 15 unit tests in-module + 22 integration tests in tests/assumptions_adversarial_decode.rs (round-trip, canonical-spelling reordering, closed-vocabulary fail-closed incl. classification/fidelity_profile/formula-kind/fragment/normal_form/action-modality, duplicate keys, truncation sweep, wrong types, W1, and two linear-size (nested-one-side-only) amplification tests targeting MAX_DEPTH/MAX_NODES). All green, clippy -D warnings clean."}	blake3:iQBUQ4F6lAouXtR7ew1afpoobVFcZ_6SLkNuhNGZmE4
1785597012585095	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy2AY		item.comment	bn-1tgp	{"body":"IMPL-04 (bounds) implemented in crates/continuum-intent/src/bounds.rs: Bounds{values,nodes,faults,depth} — no unit key, RFC 0031 classifies bounds as one tuple-shaped unit, not a keyed set. Two component types encode RFC 0037's asymmetry directly in the type system: ExplorationBound (values/depth) is Bounded(i64)|Unbounded with Unbounded the derived-Ord top (null=unbounded); DeclaredBound (nodes/faults) is Declared(i64)|Undeclared and deliberately has NO Ord impl, since a declaredness change has no direction (RFC 0031: must classify bounds unknown/fail-closed, unconditionally). Encoder always writes values/depth (null for unbounded) but omits nodes/faults entirely when undeclared (no null form exists for them in the schema) — one spelling per meaning either way, proven by decode-equivalence tests. Bounds::relation_to(&self, after) -> BoundsRelation is the typed (non-bool) comparison surface the bone asked for: {Unchanged,Expanded,Contracted,Incomparable,Unknown}, exactly RFC 0031's admissible bounds relations, with the fail-closed nodes/faults declaredness rule taking precedence over any componentwise movement. Verified directly against RFC 0031's own example ('reduce node count from five to three' -> Contracted). No diff-engine/policy-verdict/evidence work done here (change_policy's and RFC 0031's diff engine's job) — only the field's own order. Tests: 17 unit tests in-module + 14 integration tests in tests/bounds_adversarial_decode.rs (round-trip, canonical-spelling reordering, empty-object legality, unknown fields, duplicate keys, truncation sweep, wrong types incl. null rejected for nodes/faults, per-component schema minimums, and relation_to end-to-end through decode). All green, clippy -D warnings clean."}	blake3:MWpl6qZtlQC27RBSgy9-J2jg6L4gE8EF7fejLZnCWx0
1785597088013507	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy2QY		item.create	bn-3lfmi	{"description":"# Context\nFlagged by bn-136f: property.rs's formula/term JSON decoder is private, so assumptions.rs carries a second copy built from the public surface (and fairness.rs, landing in bn-14w6, likely a third). Three copies of one decoder is drift waiting to happen in a trust-boundary crate.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A pub(crate) expression-codec module (or pub(crate) surface on property.rs) that property/assumptions/fairness all import; duplicated decoders deleted.\n- [ ] Zero behavior change: all adversarial suites pass unchanged (they are the spec).\n- [ ] just check green.","kind":"task","title":"Extract shared pub(crate) expression codec in continuum-intent"}	blake3:1yGw9DFOsez-W9xR5JtAuE7vEImZX1UyeUYLAhA6Ny4
1785597096578158	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEy2gY		item.update	bn-3lfmi	{"field":"labels","value":{"action":"add","label":"req:pr-4"}}	blake3:xV1nWdGL_IHx-5kOjrpkSHlnIUmcpbiS5SZU0rX2k6A
