1785603374215160	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyAQ		item.comment	bn-mtw	{"body":"Delivered (commit 2efffca): the native protocol type layer in `crates/continuumd/src/protocol` — the crate plan §20 assigns (there is no continuum-protocol crate; START_HERE 'Dependency islands').\n\nWHAT LANDED. All 72 §10.2 operations in 18 namespace modules with typed request/response structs (138 anonymous bodies under the IDL's generated-name rule + 6 named: VerificationResult x5, TaskRecord x1), authority, annotations, verdict/events clauses, and per-operation error sets; IDL §6 envelopes (RequestEnvelope/ResultEnvelope, Error, the 4-variant Verdict union, AssuranceEnvelope); §7 handshake + protocol-major N/N-1 negotiation; §8 task records/events; §9 shared types; 33 enums incl. the complete §10.3 ErrorCode taxonomy (20 codes, @open per rule versioning.error_codes); 19 handle newtypes and 8 string aliases with their @pattern constructors. Three-valued presence is two distinct types (Nullable/Optional), so absent-vs-null cannot be conflated by accident.\n\nMECHANICALLY CHECKED, NOT GENERATED. Stated with its reversibility in the protocol module doc: no build.rs precedent exists in the workspace, and a test proves the types agree with THIS IDL now (plus RFC 0027, which a generator reading only the IDL cannot check). The check can see a renamed Rust field because protocol_struct! emits the struct field and its FieldSpec from one token — rename `components` to `component` and the spec says `component`, the IDL still says `components`, and the test names the operation, the field index, and both spellings. tests/idl_conformance.rs carries an independent IDL parser (written from the header EBNF, ~450 lines, stdlib only) and a non-vacuity self-test that mutates the IDL text across 7 drift classes + operation removal and asserts each is caught.\n\nSERIALIZATION BOUNDARY. The token layer the IDL fixes is implemented (every enum's wire spelling incl. revise-intent/bounded-schedules/heuristic-cutoff/phase-b, handle prefixes, alias patterns, presence). The byte-level canonical JSON/CBOR codec is NOT, and the module doc says why: RFC 0026 requires 'identical canonical field order' without saying what that order is (ADR-0013 is state identity, not wire layout); neither RFC nor IDL fixes union tagging; and the envelope's own Opaque payloads (arguments/payload/data) are the IDL's open item 3. Choosing those would be inventing wire format. Golden byte vectors are a conforming daemon's obligation and belong with the transport half.\n\nGATES. just check exit 0 (one full run). 55 tests across 5 files: idl_conformance 15, registry_agreement 5, closed_vocabulary_decode 6, version_window 13, adversarial_construction 16. Adversarial inputs are linear and bounded (<8192, asserted).\n\nDEPS. One workspace edge: continuum-value, because RFC 0026 says the daemon and ProtocolEpoch::negotiate/ProtocolWindow MUST agree — ProtocolVersion IS ProtocolEpoch and EpochIdentity IS that crate's type. dependency-rationale.toml used_by updated. Zero new external deps.\n\nFINDING FOR THE LEAD (not mine to fix — RFC 0026 is another agent's fence): RFC 0026 correction 15 says 'Two operations — workspace.seal and task.status — declare an empty errors clause'. The IDL declares THREE: task.subscribe has `errors [];` too. The IDL is normative, so the RFC's count and enumeration are both short by one. tests/registry_agreement.rs asserts the IDL's three and records the discrepancy inline so it cannot be lost.\n\nSEAM FOR THE DAEMON BONE: NegotiationError::error_code() returns None for MalformedRange and NoCommonEncoding — the IDL fixes no wire code for a handshake frame that is itself malformed or an encoding mismatch (MalformedRequest is defined against a request, and the handshake precedes any request envelope). That gap is documented at the call site rather than papered over.\n\nSTART_HERE: annotated the PR 5 section prose only — no bullet marked '(delivered:)', because each of the six needs its transport/behaviour half from bn-3gi/bn-18z/bn-24i. Traceability regenerated (line shifts only, no status change); validator status pass; validation-results.json byte-identical to the validator's output, so untouched."}	blake3:byH5MpSVELypzA9ffr-KwWAjI_g77b6r62Iku_ckJMU
1785603497634670	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyhgc		item.comment	bn-mtw	{"body":"Landed @ ddd7c80. Lead ran all continuumd suites in-workspace (55 tests green). Ratified: crate placement (continuumd per plan §20 + islands note); the mechanically-checked path with its diversity argument (checker parser written from the EBNF, independent of the authored types, RFC 0027 as third source); the seven-class non-vacuity mutation proof; the serialization boundary (token layer implemented, byte codec correctly deferred — canonical field order, union tagging, and Opaque payloads are unfixed by the IDL and belong to PR 5's transport half); version stays 3.0 per the recorded decision. RFC 0026 correction 15's two-vs-three discrepancy fixed trunk-direct (task.subscribe added). Authoring disclosure noted and accepted — the committed source is the reviewed artifact and the independent checker is the guarantee. NegotiationError wire-code gaps documented for the daemon bone."}	blake3:ykw8cEzCfvYubIVICUw2l_3_7HIq2mobGCbP7S_-ooY
1785603497673166	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyhwc		item.move	bn-mtw	{"state":"done"}	blake3:H12UkYMadh1m9oFYHchAK6y2NgbqxaDEA-2J0W4Jq8U
1785603497913845	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyiAc		item.comment	bn-1hg4o	{"body":"From bn-mtw: check_code_policy.py's RFC-reference rule (\\bRFC[- ](\\d{4})\\b) flags IETF RFC numbers (e.g. RFC 3339) as unresolvable Continuum RFCs — the agent worked around with 'IETF RFC3339'. Consider excluding matches preceded by 'IETF' or restricting to the 00NN range the dossier actually uses."}	blake3:nRtrGHujJg36JvpBx0TLUcRRRI4Bu8kq3OZ68hOLOL0
1785604291075706	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyAQ		item.comment	bn-n03	{"body":"continuum-kernel-sat and continuum-kernel-smt landed in workspace .maw/workspaces/bn-n03. SAT: LRAT family (RFC 0005 kernel layering; receipt kind 'lrat'), RUP steps with antecedent chains re-run by unit propagation, deletion, empty-clause requirement; RAT steps are typed Unsupported(ProofStep), never Rejected. SMT: 'smt-proof' family — atom table + propositional skeleton + theory lemmas + resolution refutation; the skeleton is fully replayed and every USED theory is named in trusted_components() with assurance_class() returning docs/03 §7's TRUSTED_SOLVER (CHECKED_CERTIFICATE when no lemma is used). No fake theory solver. Each crate depends on nothing (no workspace, no external crate), own magic (CONTSATC/CONTSMTC), same lint wall as kernel-core. 55 SAT tests, 46 SMT tests, all green; clippy -D warnings clean."}	blake3:VY4g-Oaux3RDT_-n_MBAINUyeY7M4fqPuukM9iYu2tE
1785604296476419	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyAg		item.comment	bn-15n	{"body":"continuum-kernel-temporal landed in workspace .maw/workspaces/bn-n03. Two families, both named by proof-receipt.schema.json: 'ranking' (docs/03 §6.5 Ranking; PO-LIV-002/003 — unconditional progress, every non-goal step strictly decreases a natural rank, no fairness assumption and none trusted) and 'fair-scc-exclusion' (docs/03 §6.5 Finite graph; PO-LIV-004 — kernel recomputes reachability by BFS and SCCs by iterative Tarjan over the reachable non-goal subgraph, rejecting on any weakly fair nontrivial component; the rejection is a fair-lasso witness). Strong fairness is Unsupported(FairnessClass), and a ranking that declares fair actions is Unsupported(FairnessDischarge). All three frozen Revision-2 fair-lasso spike facts (advanced.temporal_fair_lasso) are reproduced from wire form. 50 tests green; clippy -D warnings clean."}	blake3:VT3HDlaArOK1jUFGub4OBTXcqfT_Mn5812BzT-cx5pw
1785604447388250	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyiQc		item.update	bn-2ge	{"field":"labels","value":{"action":"add","label":"req:phase-a-del-07"}}	blake3:uqpKNnn14aNd7CB-hbhpKpuCwUtcXJd8PXJJk0JWvwU
1785604463511462	continuum-dev	itc:v3:AWKSTzM5JJnJPkQAAAAAQar23VW6voAAAAEyigc		item.comment	bn-n03	{"body":"Landed @ 59d2c20. Lead ran all six suites in-workspace (151 tests green). Ratified: LRAT with RAT-reserved-Unsupported (the chain-padding rejection — every antecedent must be unit — is the load-bearing strictness); SMT as skeleton-plus-named-theory-lemmas with assurance_class() deriving TRUSTED_SOLVER vs CHECKED_CERTIFICATE from lemma USE not carriage (a used lemma cannot be hidden — exactly ADR-0017's discipline); temporal's both-directions SCC-criterion proof and the overstated-fairness-weakens-claim documentation; PHASE-A-DEL-08 annotation with bn-2he as mechanical-enforcement guard. Concerns recorded: RAT + theory-lemma slices are follow-up work not defects; three-copies envelope duplication is plan §20's instruction and the biggest line-budget lever; MAX_STATES 1<<16 vs core's 1<<20 accepted pending a corpus need; cross-crate WIRE_EPOCH coordination routes to bn-2he's receipt work (INV-014). PHASE-A-DEL-07 re-covered on bn-2ge (PR 8 goal — reference-engine half)."}	blake3:5S08BmZksx-MLSPzLi5_dzreByqpUTpz5xt6p6qObxk
